{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor","id":691663,"title":"Kun-shulor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-06T13:46:57-07:00","id":691663,"title":"Kun-shulor","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SQUIDS WALK AMONG US!!!!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They come </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>from the depths</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and have infiltrated our Natural Human Society for MANY years! I have REAL and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>PHOTOGRAPHIC</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> EVIDENCE to back up these claims which I present at the end of my intelligent presentation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Many try to discount</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the squid-theory because the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">infiltrators</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> have already EATEN THEIR BRAINS!! This is what the squids want they want to EAT BRAINS for and send the CONSUMED HUMAN MEMORIES to their </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>ENSHRINED OVERLORD</u></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> AT THE BOTTOM OF THE OCEAN</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>DO NOT BELIEVE ANYONE WHO SAYS SQUIDS ARE NOT IN TRUTH THEY ARE ALREADY HERE AND THEY ARE EATING OUR SUPERIOR HUMAN THOUGHTS TO EXALT THEIR OWN KIND AND THEY MUST BE OUSTED BEFORE THEY GIVE US THE WRONG EDUCATION</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">HOW TO IDENTIFY\u2014They can look human but have 4 squid forms! 4 is their SACRED NUMBER. They can become the man-squid like described by Gygax (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>he spoke the truth and had his brain eaten!</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), the squid-as-we-know-it (clever hiders! avoid gulfs!), the Kraken (big squids STOLEN FROM OUR OWN MYTHS), and the Abomination (can\u2019t name, can\u2019t describe). THEY ALL KNOW YOUR THOUGHTS!!!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">IMPORTANT:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>They can regrow their limbs. Like the RED DEVIL they have HOOKS on their TENTACLES. They have blinding ink to get away from righteous humans.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>THEY ARE NOT GODS. THEY HAVE A WEAKNESS. . .</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Who is the Deep Overlord? NOBODY KNOWS NOT EVEN THE </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>SQUIDS</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">!!! They have theories though. This is what one told me: that there are </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>4</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> main schools of thought (HA! Squids do not think but only steal our HUMAN THOUGHTS!)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4 COMES UP AGAIN!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Is the OVERLORD trapped below Antarctica or is it just hiding??? They do not know and will not tell. If they do not obey the OVERLORD they will go </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>INSANE</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">!!!!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">THEIR GOD WILL EAT THEM BEFORE IT EATS US!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do you remember a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Bloop</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">? THAT WAS THEIR </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>GOD</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">! Evil, ignorant scientists want to keep you from the real and only TRUTH!! The Overlord Will Destroy The World When It Wakes Up! Squids make their Overlord strong by FEEDING IT OUR HUMAN BRAINS. DO NOT BELIEVE THEIR LIES THEY ARE NOT KEEPING THEIR GOD ASLEEP THAT IS RIDICULOUS AND WHAT THE GOVERNMENT-ILLUMINATI-CHEIRON-MACHINE WANTS YOU TO BELIEVE.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SATAN IS A SQUID THE GOAT IS A </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>LIE!!!!!!</u></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How do we keep ourselves safe from such a menace????????? The </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>President</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Knows And Is Doing NOTHING Because He Is Their </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Puppet</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>(President = Puppet = </u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>SQUID Logic)</u></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SQUIDS SHOULD NOT WALK AND YET THEY DO. . . THEY ARE </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>JEALOUS</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> OF OUR SUPERIOR HUMANITY. . . .</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Are they aliens?</u></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That Cannot Be Answered Until They Are Eradicated. That Secret Is Too Dark Underwater For Now.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Do they control time?</u></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They Could Not Hope To Control Time Because Squids Do Not Understand Clocks. Show A Squid A Clock And It Will Grow Confused And Afraid. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Then Is How You Will Know Your Beloved Parent Or Child Is A Squid And You Should KILL IT!</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>What do they eat?</u></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">BRAINS!! And They Drink Mercury, Mercury Poisoning In Tuna Is Squid Tampering.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>How else can I protect myself?</u></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes They Will Flash Red Like Their Red Devils And They Will Always Look Calm They Can Shunt Their Emotions Onto Others And Trade Thoughts With Anyone. REMEMBER: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Anyone Who Smells Fishy Is Probably Squid!</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I will broadcast my Message to anyone who can see it and hopefully the World is still full of Intelligent People who will understand my true and real knowledge.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>THESE WORDS WILL PROTECT YOU. . . .</u></i></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T14:06:12-07:00","id":691703,"title":"","content":"I was skeptical at first, but you make a strong argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T14:28:37-07:00","id":691715,"title":"","content":"...I'm actually kind of frightened... but also intrigued...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T00:09:42-07:00","id":692073,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, but how does this Host affect the Gauntlet? The Azlu make it too thick, the Beshilu gnaw it apart and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/419096-ukusgualu-the-lamprey-hosts\"><b>Ukusgualu</b></a> liquefy it. To follow the the imagery of monstrous cephalopods that strangle people and ships alike with their horrible tentacles, these squid hosts could drag humans and spirits from one side of the Gauntlet to the other, and imprison them there. There is a Numen in 1ED called Abduct which does that, but it only works on mortals. Of note is that a Host's mode of operation is based on its origin in Pangea. What was their progenitor spirit like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T02:44:41-07:00","id":692172,"title":"","content":"Worm hosts decay human morality/integrity, and wolf hosts scare and prey on people, so squid hosts don't need to be about the gauntlet either.<br /> <br /> That being said, I could see them be a metaphorical flood- perhaps their presence produces a watery ectoplasm that draws spirits of the appropriate essence like flies to rotting meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T03:13:23-07:00","id":692184,"title":"","content":"The original post made me think of squid changers instead of squid hosts. For example, they have five forms equivalent to those of Uratha.<br /> <br /> The brain eating thing then either has something to do with their diet (which for Uratha is flesh ), their ban (which for Uratha is hunting), or their means of reproduction.<br /> Or maybe even all of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T06:17:29-07:00","id":692322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor?p=692184#post692184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">l<br /> The brain eating thing then either has something to do with their diet (which for Uratha is flesh ), their ban (which for Uratha is hunting), or their means of reproduction.<br /> Or maybe even all of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might also be a cultural thing; Tinfoil Bob up there did take the time to deny that they do it in order to keep their progenitor from waking up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:36:31-07:00","id":692519,"title":"","content":"Please, disregard this post @.@<br /> <img src=\"http://www.godisageek.com/wp-content/uploads/Octodad.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T10:31:47-07:00","id":694002,"title":"","content":"<i>Nuku kudur, nuku shulor</i>.<br /> <br /> The words vibrate inside your head like a drive-by migraine, and then you're different from you were before. The ocean swallows you whole but you do not drown. Your body changes. Your bones soften into nothingness. Your hands split into diverse tendrils. The waves subsume you as the Deep Maker adopts you as its own child.<br /> <br /> Weresquids are real and they walk among us.<br /> <br /> BRIEF HISTORY OF THE TIME BEFORE<br /> <br /> The <i>Kun-shulor</i> aren't tied to Luna like their canine cousins are, at least not directly. Their gift and curse of shapechanging comes from the Deep Maker, an entity that dwells in one of the deepest parts of the Earth's oceans, near Antarctica. When certain psychically-sensitive individuals set foot in the ocean at the right place at the right time, the Deep Maker can feel them, and sends out a call. In this direct communion with a powerful spiritual being, the hapless individual is infused with the Deep Maker's Essence on a fundamental level, taking on some of its aspects, including shapeshifting, a spirit nature, telepathy, and. . . certain hungers.<br /> <br /> The <i>Kun-shulor</i> have four auspices, keyed to the tidal cycle: Flood, High, Ebb, and Low.<br /> <br /> WHAT IS IT LIKE TO BE A SQUID?<br /> <br /> Like the <i>Uratha</i>, weresquids have five forms. There is the <i>hishu</i>, sometimes called the &quot;diving suit&quot; among those with high Primal Urge and/or low Harmony, the <i>fa'ra</i>, which looks like a rubbery-skinned humanoid with a cephalopod head, the <i>kirul</i>, a hybrid monstrosity, the <i>kafu'ul</i>, a particularly large squid, and the <i>adalku</i>, a squid that generally resembles <i>Dosidicus gigas</i>. In these last three forms, the <i>Kun-shulor</i> has hooked tentacles (plus beak &amp; radula) that inflict lethal damage, can breathe underwater, and possesses particular resistance to blunt trauma, decreasing by two any damage received from punches, baseball bats, lead pipes, and so on. In <i>hishu</i> and <i>fa'ra</i> forms, the weresquid can hold his breath for a number of minutes equal to his Stamina + Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> In a water-breathing form, weresquids can survive in fresh and brackish waters just as easily as they can in saltwater. The <i>kirul</i> form can breathe both air and water, while the <i>kafu'ul </i>and <i>adalku</i> can hold their breath for Stamina + Primal Urge minutes.<br /> <br /> In a water-breathing form, a weresquid can emit a cloud of ink. On land, this does little, but this can muddle a body of liquid, obscuring sight and creating an opportunity for escape or ambush. The cloud lasts for Strength + Stamina turns and is the same size as the weresquid's current form. Treat the ink cloud like an Environmental Tilt.<br /> <br /> THE DARK LORD'S TERRIBLE WILL<br /> <br /> The Deep Maker stays in telepathic communion with its progeny. At any time, a weresquid might suddenly experience tinnitus accompanied by a strong instinct toward a certain action. Steal that key, investigate that human, murder that werewolf. Every time a weresquid follows the will of the Deep Maker, she receives a special kind of beat called a Deep Beat. Five Deep Beats make a Deep Experience. Deep Experiences can be spent on Gifts, Rites, Primal Urge, Skills or Merits that are directly related to an aquatic or spiritual existence. Deep Experiences can also purchase Fetishes, at a cost of one DE per dot, or Talens, at a flat cost of one DE, with a rating equal to or less than the weresquid's primary Renown. These objects will be found by the <i>Kun-shulor</i> washed up on shore, like flotsam or jetsam.<br /> <br /> Continuous unquestioning obedience to the Deep Maker eventually causes Harmony loss, as the weresquid becomes an extension of his creator's will. Disobeying the Deep Maker's instincts risks Harmony gain.<br /> <br /> A HUNGER FOR KNOWLEDGE<br /> <br /> Every weresquid is telepathic. Establishing a psychic link with another person requires a point of Willpower and an Intelligence + Wits roll, contested by Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance. If the link is established, the <i>Kun-shulor</i> can read the subject's thoughts, and automatically learns of any mental or emotional Conditions or Tilts the subject possesses. By spending a point of Essence, a weresquid can take one of these Conditions or Tilts from her subject, experiencing it instead. By spending a point of Essence and making an Intelligence + Presence vs Resolve + ST roll, the weresquid can shunt one of her own Conditions or Tilts onto the subject.<br /> <br /> In <i>fa'ra</i> or <i>kirul</i> form, a weresquid can, after successfully establishing a grapple, eat a person's brain. This grants the squid five points of Essence. Then roll Intelligence + Primal Urge (add two dice if the weresquid possesses the Eidetic Memory merit). For every success, the weresquid may ask one question that the victim's thoughts or memories could answer (&quot;What did this person see last night at nine o'clock?&quot; &quot;What was the worst thing this person has ever done?&quot; Etc.). Eating brains is a breaking point toward Spirit.<br /> <br /> NEXT TIME: SQUID GIFTS, A ROUGHSHOD SOCIETY, AND THE FEEDING FRENZY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 10-08-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T12:00:38-07:00","id":695219,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted Illithid in my WoD. Thank you for this, thank you so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:50:23-07:00","id":696346,"title":"","content":"GIFTS FOR THE GIFTED<br /> <br /> The <i>Kun-shulor</i> can receive Gifts, though the spiritual powers available to them are of a different variety. They cannot obtain Moon or Wolf Gifts, and the Gifts of Dominance and Rage are also verboten to them. Instead, they have access to Squid Gifts, which can be purchased the same way <i>Uratha</i> purchase Wolf Gifts. There are four known Squid Gifts: Flayer's Gift, Gift of Ink, Gift of Tendrils, and Gift of the Depths.<br /> <br /> Weresquids possess Renown, but they only have four categories, not five. Renown represents a weresquid's standing with the Deep Maker, and serves as an indicator of the sorts of tasks given to the <i>Kun-shulor</i>. A weresquid may have Cunning, Honor, Purity, and Wisdom, but never Glory, for they are a subtle breed. Because of this, Squid Gifts do not possess a Glory Facet, and weresquids cannot acquire the Glory Facet of any Shadow Gift.<br /> <br /> A SOCIETY OF TENTACLES<br /> <br /> A pack of weresquids is called a shoal. If one were to engage in a bit of equivocation, one might note that <i>Dosidicus gigas</i> hunts in a socializes in a manner similar to certain lupine species. Gifts or Rites that affect a pack instead affect a shoal when utilized by the <i>Kun-shulor</i>.<br /> <br /> Shoals are a bit less formal than packs, for a few reasons: First, as mentioned above, the Deep Maker values subtlety, and so the sorts of expansive packs that the <i>Uratha</i> are given over to aren't as valuable to the <i>Kun-shulor</i> (though sometimes the Deep Maker tasks one of its progeny with setting up a cult, but that's a different story). Second, there is no wolf-blood equivalent. No one has come across any squid-blooded individuals that might be of service to a shoal. Third is the feeding frenzy; close bonds are a little risky when you can never be one-hundred percent certain your friends won't flip out and try to eat you. Finally, weresquids don't have tribes, and so lack a great deal of the <i>Uratha</i>'s cultural baggage that might otherwise hold a society together.<br /> <br /> Despite the lack of tribe-analogue, weresquids do often align themselves according to various philosophies surrounding what the Deep Maker is, what its ultimate goal might be, and whether or not bringing this about is a good thing.<br /> <br /> THE FEEDING FRENZY<br /> <br /> The <i>Kun-shulor</i> do not suffer from the inner rage of the <i>Uratha</i>. In place of <i>kuruth</i> they feel a blind hunger, like when one is gorging on a large bag of potato chips, uncaring of taste or health or cleanliness, stuffing chips into one's mouth before finishing chewing and swallowing the last batch.<br /> <br /> While in a feeding frenzy, a weresquid becomes quite indiscriminate in his consumption. If it's flesh, he'll try to stuff it in his gullet. He'll use his tentacles to tear chunks of meat out of anyone around him. He'll go for the brain, if possible. The goal isn't to kill, but to consume, so victims are sometimes left alive, albeit gouged and traumatized. Being part of a bonded shoal will not stop a weresquid from turning on his fellows to partake of their mutable flesh.<br /> <br /> Whether this condition is an oversight on the Deep Maker's part, or somehow fits into the progenitor's complex, overarching scheme, remains a mystery.<br /> <br /> Weresquids have defined hunger triggers, like a werewolf's rage triggers. Staying too long in <i>kirul</i>, telepathic contact with a weresquid in frenzy, and dramatically failing certain rolls can also provoke a feeding frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 10-11-2015, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T08:53:15-07:00","id":700936,"title":"","content":"DAMP RITUALS<br /> <br /> Weresquids can learn rites, though the parameters differ. For one, certain rituals are pointless for them to use, though some come in modified versions for their special needs; for instance, there's no need for Chain Rage since weresquids don't suffer from <i>kuruth</i>, but there is a parallel rite called Bind Hunger to tamp down the Feeding Frenzy. Weresquids don't have quite the same rapport with Lunes that werewolves do, so Messenger works by beseeching the Deep Maker to open a one-way telepathic channel with the subject of the rite. And so on.<br /> <br /> The <i>Kun-shulor</i> don't get to customize their rites the same way the <i>Uratha</i> do, because of their singular attachment to the Deep Maker. When undertaking a rite, the ritemaster rolls Mental Attribute + Occult. Which Mental Attribute is determined by how the symbols are gathered.<br /> <br /> Intelligence: The weresquid must have previously experienced the symbols. During the rite she recalls these experiences and interprets their meaning.<br /> <br /> Wits: The weresquid must create the symbols for the rite, such as drawing them or employing appropriate objects.<br /> <br /> Resolve: The weresquid must clear his mind of all distractions, turning each symbol into a sort of inner mantra, imagining each one clearly, as well as the holistic connections between all symbols in the rite.<br /> <br /> As one might gather, <i>Kun-shulor</i> rites tend to be quiet, contemplative affairs, the participants' minds focused on the Deep Maker, tentacles writhing in concentration. All that silent, closed-eyes meditation does leave them open to ambush, unfortunately, as the Lodge of the Harpoon has duly noted.<br /> <br /> If all that's too much work, the ritemaster can just consume the brain of an individual that has a connection to the rite's symbols. For instance, Twilight Purge incorporates the symbols for sight, mirrors, corrosion, and the sun. A weresquid might complete this rite by eating the brain of a tanned model who's terrified of growing old and losing her beauty. Eating an appropriate brain for a rite allows the ritemaster to use his highest Mental Attribute, provides a +2 bonus to the roll, and cuts the time between rolls in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 10-21-2015, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T09:09:45-07:00","id":700956,"title":"","content":"Re@Damp Rites: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Y9o0p.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T20:28:57-07:00","id":704225,"title":"","content":"LIMBS. LIKE ARMS AND OTHER THINGS.<br /> <br /> First, a clarification of terms: For ease of reference, scientists often make a distinction between a squid's appendages: The eight shorter limbs are arms, while the two longer, penduncled ones are tentacles. Technically speaking, they're all tentacles though. Consider the terms interchangeable here (when in the appropriate form; human arms are still human arms).<br /> <br /> The Deep Maker made a taxonomical mistake, or maybe it just cherry picked its favorite traits form different cephalopods. Unlike normal squids, and more like octopods, weresquids can regrow their limbs, faster than the <i>Uratha</i> can, even. By spending a point of Essence as an instant action, the regeneration process begins. An arm or leg takes about 12 hours to fully regrow, half an arm/leg takes 6 hours, a hand or foot takes 2 hours, and a finger or toe takes 1 hour.<br /> <br /> The suckers that line a <i>Kun-shulor</i>'s tentacles are themselves lined with razor-sharp teeth. Attempting to grapple a weresquid is almost always a mistake.<br /> <br /> Newly-transformed <i>Kun-shulor</i> are often maladroit with wielding their tentacles for the first few shifts; the sensations are strange and alien, the human brain has to adjust for all the new nerve endings.<br /> <br /> In <i>fa'ra</i>, a weresquid has tentacles only around his mouth, while the <i>kirul</i> form has both mouth-tentacles, and two human-esque arms that end in clusters of them. Two longer, penduncled appendages sprout from approximately the <i>kirul</i>'s shoulder blades.<br /> <br /> What else can a weresquid do with all these new limbs? Well. . .<br /> <br /> GIFT OF TENDRILS<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning:</b> The weresquid can voluntarily detach a limb by reflexively spending a point of Essence. The process is both painless and bloodless. This is good for escaping traps, falling boulders, and the jaws of enraged Blood Talons.<br /> <br /> <b>Honor:</b> By wrapping a tentacle around a living being, the weresquid can drain them of their vital spark. Spend 1 Essence and roll Dexterity + Larceny + Honor vs Stamina + Primal Urge. Every net success deals one point of Lethal damage to the victim, and heals the user of one point of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity:</b> The weresquid gains some of the puissance of the krakens of myth. He adds his Purity rating to all grapple rolls, and can reflexively spend a point of Essence to reroll a grapple action.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> The weresquid's tentacles pierce the Gauntlet, dragging her prey from one realm to the other. The <i>Kun-shulor</i> must somehow be aware of a target on the other side of the Gauntlet from her to use this Facet. She spends 2 Essence and rolls Strength + Occult + Wisdom (+/- Gauntlet Rating) - Defense. On a success, the target is pulled through the Gauntlet to the weresquid's side. On an exceptional success, the weresquid may immediately make one grapple move of her choice on the prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:27:37-07:00","id":711186,"title":"","content":"IT'S FULL OF DHA. YOU NEED THAT TO BE HEALTHY.<br /> <br /> Cerebrophagy is a touchy subject among weresquids. The instinct to consume is strong, but for all but the most unbalanced of the <i>Kun-shulor</i>, the revulsion of taboo is (usually) stronger. Many get their first taste of gray matter during an unfortunate episode of feeding frenzy. To the weresquid palate, brains, specifically human (and human-seeming) brains taste good. Very good. Often, after the first few feedings, the excuses start to pile up. He was a serial killer. She wasn't cooperating and I needed the information. He looked at me funny. I've never had Quebecois before. It's what the Deep Maker wants.<br /> <br /> As mentioned previously, a weresquid must be in either <i>fa'ra</i> or <i>kirul</i> to consume a person's brain (straight from the head anyway). First, he must establish a grapple. Then he must perform a special new grapple move called Consume Brain. In <i>fa'ra</i>, the weresquid must use this move three times in a row to fully extract the brain, while as the monstrous <i>kirul</i>, he needs only a single turn of insertion. When performing the Consume Brain move, the weresquid wraps his buccal tentacles around the victim's head and digs into the back of the skull. Every turn that the weresquid uses the Consume Brain move, he inflicts his net successes in lethal damage as he opens up his victim's head. This does mean that certain beings with powerful enough regeneration can stall or even completely deter a <i>Kun-shulor</i>'s efforts. A human that somehow survives a brain-eating attempt will require immediate hospitalization and intensive care, followed by innumerate psychotherapy sessions.<br /> <br /> As also mentioned previously, when a weresquid consumes a person's brain, he gains five points of Essence and then rolls Intelligence + Primal Urge, with each success allowing him to ask one question that the victim's memories could answer. Brains are also incredibly nutritious for the <i>Kun-shulor</i>; consuming one alleviates all dietary needs for the next 24 hours. Brains can also function as rite symbols, to restate something else also mentioned above.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to segue for a moment, a weresquid's Bone trait is called Brain instead (squids don't have bones, you see. . .). It otherwise functions like Bone in werewolves (Blood, incidentally, also functions like Blood in werewolves, though names and popular archetypes differ; maybe Fox is called Octopus? You can probably figure this out for yourself.). Additionally, if a weresquid consumes the brain of someone whose personality lines up with his Brain trait, the <i>Kun-shulor</i> recovers all spent Willpower points.<br /> <br /> Consuming the brains of monsters can have all sorts of strange side-effects. The exact effects should be left up to Storyteller discretion, but here are some useful notes:<br /> <br /> Some Prometheans and high-Sekhem mummies might not possess brains proper. This is definitely an unpleasant surprise. Trying to eat a mummy's brain is usually a bad idea anyway, what with sealing the flesh, death curses, resurrection, and the Arisen's vindictive streak.<br /> <br /> Vampire brains are edible, but not very good. They only restore a single point of Essence, and count only as a single, poor-tasting meal for dietary purposes. Old vampires do know all sorts of interesting things, though. Also, vampires don't need their brains to live in the same way that non-vampires do. Having their brains eaten inflicts two points of aggravated damage (and can still be psychologically traumatic), but does not outright kill the vampire. With time and blood, the undead cerebellum will grow back. Neonates might risk Humanity loss from the experience, however. On Hong Kong Island, a ranking member of the Ordo Dracul named Victoria Zhou has been collaborating with a local shoal, allowing them to occasionally consume her brain for whatever odd ritual purposes they need it for, in exchange for information and insight into the <i>Kun-shulor</i> condition. She's working on a Protean Devotion that will let her mimic certain aspects of their anatomy. Her current research project is to figure out how much Vitae exists in an adult human brain.<br /> <br /> Consuming a Sin-Eater's brain will kill her permanently, as that's too much integral trauma for a Geist to work off. However, the weresquid has to get through the Bound's Plasm reserves first, which is often more effort than it's worth. Usually. If the weresquid eats the brain of a high-Synergy Sin-Eater, he can asks questions of the Geist's memories as well.<br /> <br /> In their biomechanical forms, demons have no brain to consume, or at the very least, no brain a weresquid can consume. Demons who realize what's going on will quickly shed all pretense of humanity to ensure their continued survival. If one of the Unchained is caught off guard though, they have one last defense: Roll the demon's Cover rating against the weresquid's brain interrogation roll. If the demon gains more successes, all the memories the weresquid can access come from the eaten Cover. The deceased demon's Primum will fabricate memories as need be.<br /> <br /> Weresquids can't eat the brains of ephemeral beings like spirits or angels. Animal brains, by and large, do nothing for the <i>Kun-shulor</i>, though cryptids, Hedge beasts, and other sapient fauna might be exceptions.<br /> <br /> FLAYER'S GIFT<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning</b>: With skin-to-skin contact, the weresquid can read someone's surface thoughts without the need for telepathic intrusion.<br /> <br /> <b>Honor</b>: Facets that target members of the <i>Kun-shulor</i>'s shoal can also target individuals in telepathic contact with the weresquid.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity</b>: The weresquid can directly assault the minds of others with psychic overload. She spends a point of Essence and rolls Presence + Occult + Purity (add three dice if she is already in telepathic contact with her target), contested by Resolve + Primal Urge. Every net success inflicts a point of bashing damage and strips the target of a point of Willpower. Someone reduced to zero Willpower this way gains the Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom</b>: Add the <i>Kun-shulor</i>'s Wisdom as automatic successes when sifting through the memories of a consumed brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 10-23-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:14:27-07:00","id":713269,"title":"","content":"Whelp, this is properly terrifying. Good job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:57:14-07:00","id":713333,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><i>Below the thunders of the upper deep;<br /> Far, far beneath in the abysmal sea,<br /> His ancient, dreamless, uninvaded sleep<br /> The Kraken sleepeth: faintest sunlights flee<br /> About his shadowy sides: above him swell<br /> Huge sponges of millennial growth and height;<br /> And far away into the sickly light,<br /> From many a wondrous grot and secret cell<br /> Unnumbered and enormous polypi<br /> Winnow with giant arms the slumbering green.<br /> There hath he lain for ages and will lie<br /> Battening upon huge sea-worms in his sleep,<br /> Until the latter fire shall heat the deep;<br /> Then once by man and angels to be seen,<br /> In roaring he shall rise and on the surface die.</i></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Terrible Tide's Call<br /> <b>Power:</b> 8<br /> <b>Finesse:</b> 8<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 7<br /> <b>Description: </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://orig11.deviantart.net/ccd8/f/2011/355/0/c/kraken_by_elmisa-d4ju669.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Bane:</b> Electricity.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Each hour after the first 8 without being able to submerge itself, the totem loses 1WP and 1E.<br /> <b>Pack Ban:</b> Each Week, the pack must send remains of their preys into the deep. Failure on a member to do so means the pack as a whole must make a sacriface in that fashion.<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Purify the shore.<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Water 3, Depths 1.<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Twilight Form, Reaching, Shadow Gateway, Materialize<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Spiked Tentacle Swipe), Drain, Immensity\u00b6, Clasp\u00b6, Ensnare\u00b6, Heal\u00b6<br /> <b>Heal:</b> The spirit can heal others wounds, typically for a hefty price. The spirit expends a point of Essence and rolls Power + Finesse. Bashing damage is healed before lethal, and all lethal damage must be healed before aggravated damage. Each success heals a level of bashing damage, while two successes can heal a point of lethal damage. The lethal damage healed can be used to mend aggravated damage, but each point of aggravated damage cured costs one additional point of Essence. (Healing two aggravated wounds calls for four successes and three points of Essence.) This Numen may also be used to help a character fight off disease or the effects of poison each success adding to the characters resistance rolls on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <b>Immensity:</b> By spending 5 essence points the spirit can double in Size until the end of scene. This added size adds to the spirit's corpus. Attacking beings with 10 cathegories of size less than it grants the 8 again quality to the attack.<br /> <b>Clasp:</b>This Numen allows the spirit to lock a target in a crushing embrace. The Numen functions like any brawling attack. If in the physical world, the spirit must be Materialized to affect a material target; otherwise, this Numen can only be used on other spirits in Twilight. The spirit may roll Power + Finesse when grappling instead of Power alone. (This takes the place of any Strength + Brawl rolls; see the World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 157). If the spirit spends one point of Essence, the spirits grappling attacks inflict lethal instead of bashing damage for the rest of the scene.<br /> <b>Ensnare: </b>The spirit possesses an entangling attack, be it mystic webbing, gobbets of intestine, wire mesh or glue-like spittle. To hit its target, the spirit makes a Finesse roll the targets Defense (armor does not add to Defense in this instance. Subjects struck by the attack are automatically grappled (see the World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 157). Each turn the victim may roll Strength + Athletics the spirits Power to escape; otherwise she is immobilized. After a number of turns equal to the spirits Resistance, begin reducing the effective Power of the snare by two each turn. This attack costs one point of Essence. Additional Essence may be spent to add to the snare.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T08:40:28-07:00","id":719377,"title":"","content":"While it's too early to tell for second edition, in first edition all changelings would have edible brains.<br /> <br /> Changelings can be affected by human disease, age, have their blood drunk by a vampire, don't change genetically, and possibly even sire children, the fact that a changeling's mien might not have reproductive organs, blood, cells, or DNA just isn't relevant, the changeling has all of the above anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:13:33-07:00","id":719553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor#post691663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>THEY ARE NOT GODS. THEY HAVE A WEAKNESS. . .</i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Soy Sauce?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:19:32-07:00","id":720122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor?p=719377#post719377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While it's too early to tell for second edition, in first edition all changelings would have edible brains.<br /> <br /> Changelings can be affected by human disease, age, have their blood drunk by a vampire, don't change genetically, and possibly even sire children, the fact that a changeling's mien might not have reproductive organs, blood, cells, or DNA just isn't relevant, the changeling has all of the above anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna reference this whenever someone asks if Uratha eating them should or shouldn't cause Aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:01:23-07:00","id":720295,"title":"","content":"So are these guys going to have gifts or something more along the lines of psychic powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:53:50-07:00","id":721466,"title":"","content":"TALES OF THE ABYSS<br /> <br /> You can visit the Deep Maker, if you really want to. It's not recommended, but you can do it.<br /> <br /> The Deep Maker inhabits a cave in the benthic zone of the physical world, in the Pacific Ocean at approximately the same latitude as Tierra del Fuego. It can't leave its trench, which might not be exactly as deep as Marianas Trench, but is still pretty dark. In fact, only a relatively small portion of the Deep Maker's titanic body can be glimpsed; the rest is sealed off behind layers of rock, with only scores of tentacles and radulae and a few hundred meters of mutable flesh to be appreciated.<br /> <br /> There's also everything else making an honest living down there.<br /> <br /> The Deep Maker's trench is full of its various flesh- and Essence-shaping experiments. The choicest examples of abyssal gigantism can be found, colossal squids and deepwater stingrays and kings of herrings to rival anything anywhere else on the planet. The Gauntlet here is thin, and the trench itself is a 5-dot locus, and so many spirits of the deep sea have crossed over, either on their own whims or at the Deep Maker's behest. Sometimes it takes spirits and shoves them inside a convenient animal host, creating new and interesting types of Claimed. Sometimes it reaches out fuses two animals together, creating fleshy versions of the <i>magath</i>. Its favored guardians appear to be goblin sharks blended with Nomura's jellyfish.<br /> <br /> But anyway, if you make it down far enough you can find the Deep Maker, trapped away in its enormous cave, tentacles waving haphazardly, though sometimes also rhythmically.<br /> <br /> It seems to be sleeping.<br /> <br /> Is everything it's doing just the by-product of some mad dream?<br /> <br /> Mental contact with the Deep Maker, whether through telepathy or the Mind Arcanum or Auspex or oneiromancy or what-have-you, inflicts a persistent Madness Condition. This does not mean the attempt is a failure, though. The Deep Maker's thoughts are just incredibly alien and disturbing.<br /> <br /> Occasionally a weresquid will receive a strong instinct from the Deep Maker to dive into the ocean and join it in its abyssal trench. These chosen few are never seen or heard from again.<br /> <br /> SO WHAT IS IT?<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> Before Mother Luna was courted by Father Wolf, she dallied with the dwellers in the sea of all types. The tides danced at her call at the deeps were her special, private playground, existing in a place where the distance of the stars above wrapped around into the waters below. But when Urfarah came, he would not brook the trespass of any rival suitor, and so he shredded the dwellers of the deep in his terrible jaws and collapsed their underwater kingdoms into so much rubble so he could beget his spawn in peace.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> When Mother Wolf and Father Luna sealed away the idigam, one such impossible beast hid in the only way it knew: between the cracks of reality. The creature concealed itself as far away from the moon's harsh gaze as it could, and now passes the time, waiting for that heavenly body to crash into its new abode, for this will happen eventually. Eventually. It's made certain of it.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> The universe is home to so many things beyond mortal ken. In ancient times, when the Earth was still young, one came from a distant star seeking new terrains to explore. It found our world to its liking, and so settled here. The primitive peoples worshiped it like a god, and it was content with this. But then a group of so-called righteous heroes struck down its tyranny and buried it beneath the waves. And now it seeks revenge for the injustice done it and those like it.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> When Urfarah died and the Border Marches were shattered, many Pangeans perished in the chaos. Spider and Rat shattered, and Great Eagle flew to parts unknown. Many-Arms knew its time would also come if it did not act quickly, and so it gathered its essence and materialized in the World of Flesh, and found purchase in the one place it could truly call home. In time Many-Arms grew lonely and desired children. And so it made them, using the bodies of the drowned, the different, those who strayed from the safety of land into the cold embrace of sea.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> The world is ruled by a great Machine and its terrible Angels. In Its Divine Computations, the Machine figured long ago how to psychologically condition humanity into total obedience, but it required rare and valuable resources to complete its project. And lo the Machine sent one of its Glorious Archangels into the Depths to retrieve that which was necessary to its plan. But circumstances changed, and the Machine's plans changed with them, and now its Glorious Archangel lies forgotten, waiting for the day It is called into Service once again.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> The Ladder fell at the behest of a song. The song was sung from a dark corner of the world, a place seen only by the most enlightened of the wise. Time is an illusion, and the world has always been as Fallen as it is now. Do not believe their lies.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, in the mists of forgotten history, there was a woman who wanted to be a mother. But she could not. Many would resign themselves to despair, but this woman's resolve was greater than most. And so she traded dearly with a wizened creature for the secret to finding a hidden path to a distant land, a fragmented sea whose lord would surely bless her with her utmost desire. And so she traveled down, through caves and forests and abandoned cities and bloodstained battlefields, and in many moons she reached the ocean, in a land that was not a land, and met with an ever-hungry thing that had never seen true sunlight. And she told it her deepest wish. And as a reward for finding it, the lord ate her dreams and curled up inside her soul, like a false child. The mother was content with this for now, and she returned whence she came, and found that her hungers and the hungers of her child had become one, and with its aid she became a tyrannical sorcerer-queen, ruling over those who once ruled her. And the hungers grew and she found new ways to feed them. And as she fed her hungers her might grew as well, and then she began to make her own children, and called herself the Mother of All Monsters, and she gave them their own hungers to fill so they could be mothers and fathers like she. And all was well for her until a man of storms and virtue set out to strike her down, and this would not do, she still had so many things to accomplish, and so on the day of their fated battle she instead dove back into the distant, fragmented land of her monstrous soul, and the thundering king declared himself victor over her cowardice, but that did not matter because she got to survive and grow and feed ever more, ever more, happily ever after.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> When the right memory is consumed in the right place at the right time, it will awaken from its slumber and flood the world and establish a new kingdom of horror and darkness. This will be a glorious time for the <i>Kun-shulor</i>, but not so much for all the lesser servitor races.<br /> <br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> It cannot be stopped. It is already here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 10-24-2015, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T20:20:43-07:00","id":721590,"title":"","content":"That last bit sounds like a Cahalith went mad. Just repeating 'This story is true...&quot; and rambling.<br /> <br /> I like it. It fits the weresquids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T23:14:57-07:00","id":721985,"title":"","content":"What Dreaminggod said, and my personal interpretation is that these are the thoughts of the Deep Maker, either absorbed from greater beings or observed <i>first-hand</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T07:29:31-07:00","id":732230,"title":"","content":"This is fucking awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T07:44:17-08:00","id":756464,"title":"","content":"Two words...<br /> <br /> Absolutely terrific.<br /> XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:47:02-08:00","id":756893,"title":"","content":"Awesome - IS there a PDF that brings it all together, or do I need to do all that work myself?<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:46:27-08:00","id":757690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor?p=756893#post756893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome - IS there a PDF that brings it all together, or do I need to do all that work myself?<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you're making a PDF, why stop with just the Kun Shulor? Add in other cool homebrew shapeshifters like those wereotters (Kushtaka?). And didn't someone put together a stopgap 2E conversion for shapeshifters from both Changing Breed and War Against the Pure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:31:46-08:00","id":758533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor?p=757690#post757690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you're making a PDF, why stop with just the Kun Shulor? Add in other cool homebrew shapeshifters like those wereotters (Kushtaka?). And didn't someone put together a stopgap 2E conversion for shapeshifters from both Changing Breed and War Against the Pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming I were to take the effort to make a PDF, it would sadly not be 2nd Edition Compatible, as I play 1st Edition (meaning the data would change from what is already presented as I will have to back-port it for my game). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:40:31-08:00","id":758642,"title":"","content":"SQUID MOON RISING<br /> <br /> The <i>Kun-shulor</i> have auspices keyed to four tidal conditions. Whatever the tide is when one enters the water and undergoes the First Change is that weresquid's auspice. Auspice grants a primary Renown type as well as a free dot in one of three Skills. One's Auspice appears to be correlated to the sorts of tasks the Deep Maker sets out for the <i>Kun-shulor</i>.<br /> <br /> Flood Tide: As waters rise, the Direct come surging further inland, ready to swallow anything caught in their path. Renown: Purity. Auspice Skills: Athletics, Brawl, Intimidation.<br /> <br /> High Tide: The Devious lurk in dark, hidden depths, waiting to surprise the unwary, taking whatever drops into their domain. Renown: Cunning. Auspice Skills: Larceny, Stealth, Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> Ebb Tide: The Planners understand when it is time to make a calculated retreat, and discretion's computational relation to other virtues. As the tide recedes, so do they, biding their time for the opportune moment. Renown: Honor. Auspice Skills: Academics, Persuasion, Survival.<br /> <br /> Low Tide: When the waters are at their lowest, the ocean gives up some of its precious secrets, leaving flotsam and jetsam among its shores for the Crafters to pick through for their strange arts. Renown: Wisdom. Auspice Skills: Crafts, Empathy, Occult.<br /> <br /> <br /> WHAT'S LUNA GOT TO DO WITH IT?<br /> <br /> A good question. The Spirit Mother and her Lunes hold influence over the tidal choirs, the Shore-Howlers, the Cowardly Whitecaps, Uzumaki's Maw, and other Shadow denizens. It would certainly explain why the <i>Kun-shulor</i> have the same number and type of forms as the <i>Uratha</i>, as well as why they can cross the Gauntlet in the first place, despite their progenitor's completely Fleshy existence.<br /> <br /> Lunes sometimes think they can boss the <i>Kun-shulor </i>around, as if their dominion over the tides gives them dominion over the squids as well. The Deep Maker seems to be pleased when a weresquid devours one of these uppity celestials. No heavenly body can comprehend the vast hunger of the sea.<br /> <br /> Granted, eating Lunes tends to upset Luna's other children, for some reason. You'd think getting rid of the things that drive them mad would be seen as a favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 11-12-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:49:19-08:00","id":758649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor?p=700936#post700936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DAMP RITUALS</div> </div> </div> </div>These rituals are quite dank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:16:54-08:00","id":758876,"title":"","content":"GIFT OF INK<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning:</b> The weresquid can shoot a burst of ink into someone's eyes, temporarily blinding them. Spend 1 Essence and roll Dexterity + Athletics + Cunning - Defense. On a success, she inflicts the Blinded Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Honor:</b> The weresquid can create a cloud of ink on land the same way he can in the water. This costs 1 Essence and creates an Environmental Tilt (perhaps something like the Darkness Lair Trait from Beast: The Primordial).<br /> <br /> <b>Purity:</b> Add the weresquid's Purity rating to the duration of his ink cloud. Additionally, for 1 Essence, the <i>Kun-shulor </i>can designate a number of individuals up to his Purity rating exempt from the obfuscating effects of his ink; they can see through it as easily as if it were water.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> With a touch, the weresquid can alter the shape of ink, including printed media. She spends 1 Essence and rolls Wits + Expression + Wisdom. On a success, the ink warps to her desire, lasting either 24 hours (for printed media and other lasting forms of ink), until the ink dissipates (such as a cloud in the water), or until the weresquid wills it otherwise (on an exceptional success). She might alter the text on a flyer, reshape a tattoo into a different design, keep an ink cloud centered on one individual, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T08:11:51-08:00","id":763125,"title":"","content":"GIFT OF THE DEPTHS<br /> <br /> (NB: Unlike other Squid Gifts, the Gift of the Depths may be acquired by other werethings as a Shadow Gift. Finding the bathypelagic spirits that can carve the Facets and convincing them to do so is another matter entirely.)<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning:</b> The weresquid becomes bioluminescent. In any form, he may emit a soft glow from his skin for no cost. The light is about as bright as a candle. In darkness, he gains one other trick: He may cause the patterns of his bioluminescence to shift deceptively and attractively. Choose a target, spend 1 Essence and roll Manipulation + Expression + Cunning - Composure. On a success, the target gains the Compulsion Condition to draw toward the strange lights.<br /> <br /> <b>Honor:</b> The weresquid no long has to worry about drowning. In every form she can breathe both water and air. Environmental penalties in water are also reduced for her by her Honor: entangling kelp, strong currents, low visibility, arctic waters, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity:</b> Abyssal gigantism is a phenomenon by which animals that inhabit the lower depths of the ocean tend to grow much larger than their shallower counterparts, such as the deepwater stingray, the king of herrings, the Japanese spider crab, or the colossal squid. Anyway, a weresquid with this Facet may, as a reflexive action, spend a point of Essence to increase her Size by 1 for the rest of the scene. She may keep spending Essence one-for-one to continue growing, gaining up to her Purity rating in Size this way.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>By reflexively spending a point of Essence, the weresquid gains a type of blindsense for the rest of the scene. He may detect things through the way they disturb the air, water, and earth around them. This works best against things that are moving; to detect the presence of immobile objects or creatures, the weresquid must succeed on a Perception roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:40:48-08:00","id":763184,"title":"","content":"Need to put here full <b>Spectre</b> Intro for mining ideas once it will be legally possible... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T15:01:13-08:00","id":765821,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Patrick opened the door to his apartment, tired from a day\u2019s work, but also satisfied, and for a moment he did not hear the music softly wafting from an anterior room. The lights in the hall and kitchen were switched off, as was his bedroom left; the only illumination came from the soft evening glow of a few west-facing windows. Patrick closed his eyes and savored the small differences between near-darkness and darkness, or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>epipelagic</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>aphotic</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> as he had spent the day describing to rapt schoolchildren, or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>creeping dread</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>mortal terror</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> as the many-limbed thing that had years ago eaten his soul liked to evoke.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It was when his eyes were closed that his ears first detected a few faint notes, an acoustic guitar\u2019s chord, accompanied by a tenor voice whose words were still inaudible. Even then for a moment Patrick thought that the music was wafting in from a neighboring residence, but a new glimmer of realization traced the sound to the living room at the end of the hallway.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Patrick felt himself tense, his nerves on high alert. The remnants of human instinct prepared his body for either fight or flight, hormonal encoders that no ethereal kraken could fully purge. The music continued; it was a vaguely-familiar melody, a song Patrick was sure he hadn\u2019t listened to in some time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The living room was also dark, save for the faint gray of twilight. As Patrick crept to the threshold, the music\u2019s sonic outline became clearer. He recognized the lyrics now, partly from their new clarity, partly from a distant memory.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A moment later he also distinguished the outline of a human figure sitting on an Ottoman in the far corner of the room. It shifted as Patrick stood on the threshold. His eyes had no need to adjust to the darkness, and so he also made out the crude paper mask affixed to the intruder\u2019s face. It had almond-shaped holes cut into it, but otherwise was featureless. The music was coming from a neighboring speaker connected to an old cd player.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cThis is my favorite song on the mix cd you gave me,\u201d the figure suddenly said, its\u2014his\u2014voice somewhat hoarse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Patrick had a moment of realization. \u201cTim?\u201d he asked, his voice somewhat nervous. This was a person he had believed he would never see again. It had been years since they had last spoken. Patrick\u2019s mouth suddenly felt and tasted as if he had just swallowed a large gulp of seawater as a faint buzzing coursed through the back of his head. This was new. The sensation cut off the \u201cFuck you, this isn\u2019t your story\u201d he was preparing to lob. His ex-lover was no Hero, but instead Kin.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This, of course, still did not answer the question of why Tim was sitting in Patrick\u2019s living room, in the dark, wearing a mask, and playing the mix cd Patrick had gifted him during their relationship.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the tense moment of silence between the two, the song ended. It was replaced by a ballad comparing amorous feelings to fermented juniper berries.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tim stood, slowly, like a wad of paper uncrumpling. His mask shifted.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cMother wants me to eat your brain,\u201d he rasped, as the first tentacles began to snake from beneath the mask, \u201cbut I\u2019d much rather eat your heart, you see.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Patrick took a step back\u2014out of surprise, he told himself, rather than actual fear\u2014as he evaluated the situation. Tim was Kin, but was he. . . \u201cMother\u201d? He didn\u2019t seem to possess a Horror, so what could he. . .</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sudden migraine cut off his train of thought. It felt like his neurons had been dipped in acid. Patrick grasped his head and fell to his knees as Tim approached. Patrick managed to look up; at some point Tim had removed the flimsy paper mask from his face. His head resembled something one would find in a deep-sea trench, or in a horror film about aliens. Maybe both. Despite the unfortunate and uncomfortable situation Patrick was in, the kraken in his soul felt a sympathy for the kind of fear this new form Tim had taken on might inspire in tremulous land-dwellers. A high-pitched grinding sensation in his occipital lobe kept Patrick from forming a coherent sentence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tim was now standing directly in front of, and above, Patrick. The modern-casual style of his jeans and flannel shirt contrasted with the rubbery appearance of his flesh, the mass of tentacles surrounding his mouth, his enlarged eyes. To Patrick\u2019s surprise, Tim\u2019s first action was to run a hand across the side of Patrick\u2019s head, brushing a lock of hair over his right ear. The look of what remained human in his face made Patrick think of longing and sadness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is true that Tim had not taken the break-up very well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For a moment, Patrick thought of Ahmed. Ahmed was busy with his own things that evening, investigating a puzzling mystery with a cadre of necromancers. Patrick hoped that he was having a much better time than he was, then wished Ahmed was there with him, then idly wondered what Tim would think of Ahmed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At that moment the sun had set just enough more to plunge the twilit room into total darkness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dark like the bottom of the sea, Patrick thought. Unbeknownst to him, Tim had thought this too, but that was of no importance right then.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Patrick closed his eyes, bowed his head, and as he felt the brush of a clammy, boneless appendage on his brow, he summoned an ocean.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Three moments later, two very large cephalopods were entangled in the lightless depths of a sea without a surface, while the last echoes of a soft melody faded.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 11-17-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T17:01:11-08:00","id":766660,"title":"","content":"Aaand that made me sad. Patrick and Ahmed were some of my favourite sample characters from the Beast drafts.<br /> <br /> Also, yay for some Deep One style werecreatures. I do like how the 2e Core makes a mention of a ludicrously powerful Idigam that may or may not be Mother Ocean from the perspective of the Brineborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:13:29-08:00","id":768514,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Kinship Nightmare: Garbled Nonsense (Weresquid)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>There\u2019s this awful ringing in your head. You can\u2019t keep anything straight. Thoughts slip out of your head before you can fully think them. Maybe you should be getting more sleep, or stronger coffee.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Intelligence + Satiety - Resolve</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Normal Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> All mental actions suffer a -3 penalty for the duration of the Nightmare.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">High Satiety:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The target\u2019s thoughts are drowned in static and staccato, besieged by bizarre imagery. Whenever the target fails a mental roll, he takes a Madness Condition that\u2019s resolved when the Nightmare ends.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Satiety Expenditure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> For the duration of the Nightmare, all information-gathering powers are also scrambled. Auspex, Omen Sensitivity, Telepathy, Clairvoyance, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, and similar abilities cannot be activated; attempting to just gives the victim a headache and tinnitus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Nightmare lasts for 24 hours.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:17:12-08:00","id":768516,"title":"","content":"<b>To-do:</b><ul><li>Merits</li> <li>Harmony</li> <li><i>Siskur-dah</i></li> <li>Philosophies</li> <li>Auspice abilities?</li> <li>Special Rites</li> <li>Fetishes</li> <li>Form traits</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T09:29:07-08:00","id":771532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/691663-kun-shulor?p=763125#post763125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GIFT OF THE DEPTHS<br /> <br /> (NB: Unlike other Squid Gifts, the Gift of the Depths may be acquired by other werethings as a Shadow Gift. Finding the bathypelagic spirits that can carve the Facets and convincing them to do so is another matter entirely.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My question about this part is what if a Werewolf learns this Gift? Is there a hidden fifth gift for the final renown? Or does it just not exist (yet)?<br /> <br /> Also when it comes to other Shadow Gifts is the fifth Facet restricted, or is there a way for them to get it (maybe if they unlock the other four they can get it? And activate it using the weakest of their Renowns? Or maybe Primal Urge/2 rounded up?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ALSO DAMN YOU!<br /> <br /> &gt;.&gt; I was writing up my own were-Cephalopods, but you've done an amazing job. &gt;.&gt; The main difference was mine was I was going to give them all five renown's (I like your idea better) and one of the Primal Urge Benefits for mine was an increase in their size when in any form that wasn't human. (They'd start as big as the Giant Pacific Octopus and end up as big as a Colossal Squid. Maybe bigger.<br /> <br /> edit: formatting\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:15:38-08:00","id":771817,"title":"","content":"As I promised - James Bond is Kun-Shulor!!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=762PPKoCYI4\" data-code=\"762PPKoCYI4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/762PPKoCYI4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> ( I think in the visualisation are nice ideas for the WereSquides Gifts - will mark them in free time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T14:22:09-08:00","id":778595,"title":"","content":"FINDING MEANING IN THE ABSURD<br /> <br /> After getting over the initial reaction that they are now a kid who is also a squid, a <i>Kun-shulor</i> has to figure out their relationship with the Deep Maker. Obeying the Maker's implanted instincts feels not unpleasant, and comes with perks, but will sooner or later put you into an awkward moral or social (or physical) position. Disobeying means you're more of your own free squid, but also comes with Harmony gain, distancing you from your spirit half, and moreover, the instincts get louder and louder as pressure builds. . .<br /> <br /> Figuring out one's existence as a cephalopodic shapeshifter revolves around two axes: The first is what doing all these things for the Deep Maker is meant to accomplish. The second is whether or not that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> A common belief among the <i>Kun-shulor</i> is that the Deep Maker is currently asleep, or trapped, or in a near-death state, and each task completed for it gives it a bit more strength, that fulfilling these instincts delivers to its underwater abode a jolt of occult Essence. Eventually, with enough deep instincts obeyed, the Maker will free itself, and do. . . something. Maybe it will return to the Shadow (or wherever it came from). Maybe it will destroy the world, or remake it in its own image, become a new god for a new age, with the weresquids as its favored servitor angels.<br /> <br /> Other <i>Kun-shulor</i> think that the Deep Maker will never break free of its oneiric prison, and so it has set up the weresquids as its abovewater agents, playing a game of cosmic chess with other powerful entities. Every strange command it sends from the depths is to accomplish some purpose mortal minds can hardly fathom, singular moves that drive forward the occult physics of the universe. Perhaps what the weresquids do is even necessary to maintain the world as it is now, and without the larceny, gaslighting, and brain-eating, things would fall apart completely.<br /> <br /> Others still, especially those who have gone to visit the Deep Maker in person, think that there is no higher purpose to all of this, that the Deep Maker has gone mad from its imprisonment, or was always a lunatic, a blind idiot god from the beginning of time, that its choosing of the weresquids is pure chance, their missions nothing but the nonsensical whims of a dead dreamer. That the <i>Kun-shulor</i> only derive spiritual power from obeying the Deep Maker because it has carved its Essence into their souls.<br /> <br /> Their are stranger beliefs still among the squids. No tribal customs or traditions bind them together, so everyone has to find their own way, from what they can piece together on their own and from what others of their kind (as well as other denizens of the World of Darkness) can tell them. No one's gone to war over what they think of the Deep Maker, but conflicts of interest do arise when you are still quite attached to humanity while the neighboring shoal has no qualms about turning your hometown into the next Innsmouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:17:36-08:00","id":816855,"title":"","content":"THE FORMS<br /> <br /> <i>Hishu</i><br /> Terrestrial<br /> Perception +1<br /> Sheep's Clothing<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Fa'ra</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dexterity +1, Stamina +1<br /> Terrestrial<br /> Consume Brain (3 rounds)<br /> Perception +2<br /> Mild Lunacy<br /> Defense vs Firearms<br /> <b>Psychic Shock:</b> A weresquid in this form can temporarily override the neural receptors in his prey's brain, leaving him exposed. The weresquid must make eye contact and roll Intelligence + Primal Urge, contested by the prey's Resolve + Primal Urge. If the weresquid wins, the prey receives the Stunned Tilt for one round.</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('di